      "title": "The Results",
      "content": "The evaluation shows that the premise order effect is significant, with a performance drop of over 30% when the premise order is altered. The **R-GSM benchmark** is introduced to examine the ordering effect on mathematical problem-solving, and the results demonstrate that all LLMs perform considerably worse on rewritten problems.",
